{"履修期": "秋学期", "主な教授言語": "英語", "授業目的": "Please refer to the English section.", "到達目標": "Please refer to the English section.", "特記事項": "", "関連科目": "", "授業の概要・背景": "<p data-path-to-node=\"4\">This is a high-level course. It is recommended that students have already taken similar advanced English courses. You will be required to understand native-level English materials and technical filmmaking concepts.</p><p data-path-to-node=\"5\">Because this is a hands-on, practical class, you must be prepared to work hard, actively collaborate in groups, and participate heavily in creative discussions. Success in this course depends on your teamwork, active participation, and willingness to experiment with film production.</p>", "授業方法": "Course Format &amp; RequirementsEnglish-Only Classroom: This is a high-level, communication-based course taught entirely in English. You will interact in English every lesson with both the teacher and your classmates through discussions, pair work, group projects, and presentations. The class functions as a community where everyone is expected to support each other.Practical Group Work: Because filmmaking is collaborative, you will work regularly in small teams to brainstorm, direct, shoot, and edit your videos. Active, hands-on participation is required.Tech &amp; Hardware Requirements: We will use Google Classroom and Google Drive for all course information and assignment submissions (both are free with a Google account). Recording can be done on your phone or you can borrow equipment from the teacher or the Organization for Information Strategies.Computer Access:&nbsp;Access to a computer is recommended (Mac, Windows desktop/laptop, or a school computer lab) to properly finish and submit your assignments. While films can be made on a smartphone, it is easier on a computer", "トピック": {"第1回": ["<div><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px;\">ALL SESSION INFORMATION IS SUBJECT TO CHANGE AT THE TEACHER'S DISCRETION</span></div><div><span style=\"font-si